Package: encryptor
Version: 2.1.0-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: mpgamer75 <mpgamer75@github.com>
Depends: openssl (>= 1.1.1), bash (>= 4.0)
Recommends: curl, wget, git, coreutils, less
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/mpgamer75/encryptor
Description: Advanced CLI encryption tool with AES-256-GCM, S/MIME, and PKI management
 Encryptor is an industry-grade command-line encryption tool built on OpenSSL.
 It provides authenticated encryption, full X.509 PKI management, and a rich
 interactive TUI — with zero dependencies beyond bash and openssl.
 .
 Security highlights in v2.1.0:
  - AES-256-GCM as default (true AEAD — confidentiality AND integrity)
  - Passwords never passed on command line (file descriptor pattern)
  - PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 with 600,000 iterations (OWASP 2024)
  - SHA-256 integrity sidecar files for tamper detection
 .
 Features:
  - Symmetric: AES-256-GCM (default), AES-256-CBC/CTR, ChaCha20, Camellia, ARIA
  - Asymmetric: S/MIME with X.509 certificates (AES-256-GCM key wrap)
  - Full PKI: Root CA creation, CSR generation, signing, PKCS#12 export
  - Security audit: 8 local checks with score + remote SSL/TLS scanning
  - Batch/non-interactive mode with JSON output for CI/CD pipelines
  - Interactive color-coded TUI with spinner and status bar
  - Secure file deletion (3-pass shred)
  - Cross-platform: Linux, macOS, WSL